<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    
    <h2>What Is the Butterfinger® Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Butterfinger® Blizzard is driven by one specific texture: the crispy, crumbly, flaky peanut-butter wafer that defines the Butterfinger candy. When blended into DQ soft serve, the wafer pieces partially dissolve into the cream while retaining enough structure to deliver crunch. The peanut butter flavor is present but lighter than the <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's Blizzard</a> — a good option for guests who want a hint of peanut butter without the intensity.</p>
  <p>Browse all Blizzard flavors and 2026 prices on <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Butterfinger vs. Reese's — Which PB Blizzard Should You Order?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose <strong>Butterfinger®</strong> if you want a lighter, crispy peanut butter crunch with fewer calories (470 cal Small). The wafer-light texture keeps the flavor from being too heavy.</li>
    <li>Choose <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard"><strong>Reese's® PB Cup</strong></a> if you want full-intensity peanut butter and chocolate. More calorie-dense at 600 cal Small but more satisfying for dedicated PB fans.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Best Time to Order the Butterfinger Blizzard</h2>
  <p>The Butterfinger Blizzard is one of the better options as a dessert after a heavier meal — it is lighter in calories than most other Blizzards while still delivering real candy-bar satisfaction. Pair it with a <a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">cheeseburger</a> and <a href="/items/regular-fries">fries</a> from the DQ food menu for a complete meal under reasonable total calories.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Butterfinger® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>470</td><td>Lightest PB-chocolate option</td></tr><tr><td>Reese's® PB Cup Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>600</td><td>Richer PB, higher calorie</td></tr><tr><td>M&amp;M's® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>490</td><td>Candy crunch, no peanut butter</td></tr><tr><td>Snickers® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>500</td><td>PB + caramel + nougat</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (3.49) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (4.49) at 470 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

